module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.Fppf.Subcanonical
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# The fpqc topology of the big fppf site over a scheme is subcanonical

The fpqc "topology" the descent arguments for algebraic spaces work with is not a chosen
system of covering families: it is the preimage
`Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage.comap (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)` of the fpqc
precoverage of all schemes along the canonical functor out of the big fppf site over `S`,
and its generated topology is what
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.Fpqc.SheafCondition` and its successors state the
sheaf condition for. This file shows that topology is *subcanonical*, so that every
representable presheaf on the site is an fpqc sheaf.

The statement is the fpqc counterpart of
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.subcanonical_topology` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.Fppf.Subcanonical`, and it is *not* proved the same
way. The fppf case is the localization `B.topology.over (B.obj hS)` of a topology on the
size-bounded category, so Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.subcanonical_over` applies directly. Here the topology is
given by a preimage along `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.toScheme`, which is **not full** —
a morphism of schemes between two objects of the site need not commute with the structure
morphisms to `S` — so the transport
`CategoryTheory.Precoverage.subcanonical_toGrothendieck_of_fullyFaithful` cannot be applied to
that functor. The two halves of `toScheme` are handled separately instead: the size-bounded
inclusion `B.inclusion` *is* fully faithful, and the slice is a plain `CategoryTheory.Over`,
for which Mathlib identifies the localized topology with the preimage topology.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.subcanonical_fpqcTopology`: the topology generated by the
  preimage of the fpqc precoverage along the size-bounded inclusion `Sch_κ ⥤ Sch` is
  subcanonical.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.fpqcTopology_eq_over`: the topology generated by the preimage
  of the fpqc precoverage along `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.toScheme` is the localization at
  `S` of the previous one. **This is the comap-to-the-slice transport.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.subcanonical_fpqcTopology`: **the fpqc topology of the big
  fppf site over `S` is subcanonical.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isSheaf_fpqc_yoneda_obj`: a representable presheaf on the big
  fppf site over `S` is an fpqc sheaf.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isSheaf_fpqc_pullback_yoneda_obj`: a fibre product of an fpqc
  sheaf over an fpqc sheaf along a morphism from a representable presheaf is an fpqc sheaf.

## Implementation notes

*Why no coverage argument is needed.* The chosen covering families of a big fppf site are only
stable under base change *up to refinement*, which is why
`CategoryTheory.Precoverage.subcanonical_toGrothendieck_of_fullyFaithful` takes the refinement
hypothesis rather than `CategoryTheory.Precoverage.IsStableUnderBaseChange`. A preimage
precoverage has no such defect: `Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage` is stable under base change and the
inclusion preserves and creates fibre products, so both
`CategoryTheory.Precoverage.IsStableUnderBaseChange` and
`CategoryTheory.Precoverage.HasPullbacks` are already instances for the preimage, and the
refinement hypothesis is discharged by the base-changed presieve itself
(`CategoryTheory.Presieve.FactorsThruAlong.pullbackArrows`). Those same two instances are what
Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.over_toGrothendieck_eq_toGrothendieck_comap_forget` asks for, which
is why the localization step is an equality of topologies and not an inequality.

*The factorisation used.* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.toScheme` is by definition
`CategoryTheory.Over.forget (B.obj hS) ⋙ B.inclusion`, so
`CategoryTheory.Precoverage.comap_comp` splits the preimage into the preimage along the
inclusion followed by the preimage along the forgetful functor of the slice. No declaration
here is a Stacks tag: subcanonicality of the fpqc topology on all schemes is Mathlib's, and
these are its transports to the site this development uses.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 021R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/021R)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 023Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/023Q)
-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

namespace BigFppfSite

/-- **The fpqc topology of a big fppf site is subcanonical.** The size-bounded inclusion
`Sch_κ ⥤ Sch` is fully faithful and preserves fibre products, and a presieve of `Sch_κ` is a
covering for the preimage precoverage exactly when its image is an fpqc covering family of
schemes, so this is Mathlib's subcanonicality of the fpqc topology on all schemes transported
along the inclusion.

The refinement hypothesis of the transport is discharged by the base-changed presieve, which
is a covering because the fpqc precoverage is stable under base change and the inclusion
creates fibre products. -/
instance subcanonical_fpqcTopology (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) :
    (Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage.comap B.inclusion).toGrothendieck.Subcanonical :=
  Precoverage.subcanonical_toGrothendieck_of_fullyFaithful _ Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage
    B.inclusion le_rfl fun f R hR ↦
      ⟨Presieve.pullbackArrows f R, Precoverage.pullbackArrows_mem f hR,
        Presieve.FactorsThruAlong.pullbackArrows f R⟩

end BigFppfSite

namespace BigFppfOver

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- **The comap-to-the-slice transport for the fpqc precoverage.** The topology generated by
the preimage of the fpqc precoverage along `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.toScheme` is the
localization at `S` of the topology generated by the preimage along the size-bounded
inclusion.

`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.toScheme` factors as the forgetful functor of the slice
followed by the inclusion, so the preimage splits by
`CategoryTheory.Precoverage.comap_comp`, and Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.over_toGrothendieck_eq_toGrothendieck_comap_forget` identifies the preimage
along the forgetful functor of a slice with the localization — the preimage precoverage being
stable under base change and having pullbacks. -/
theorem fpqcTopology_eq_over :
    (Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage.comap (toScheme B S hS)).toGrothendieck =
      (Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage.comap B.inclusion).toGrothendieck.over (B.obj hS) := by
  rw [over_toGrothendieck_eq_toGrothendieck_comap_forget, ← Precoverage.comap_comp]

/-- **The fpqc topology of the big fppf site over `S` is subcanonical.** This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.subcanonical_fpqcTopology` localized at `S`, through
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.fpqcTopology_eq_over` and Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.subcanonical_over`. -/
@[sga "3 IV 6.3.1" "(iii), special case", sga "3 XV 8.10" "(i)", sga "4 VII 4.2" "special case"]
instance subcanonical_fpqcTopology :
    (Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage.comap (toScheme B S hS)).toGrothendieck.Subcanonical := by
  rw [fpqcTopology_eq_over]
  infer_instance

/-- **A representable presheaf on the big fppf site over `S` is an fpqc sheaf.** This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.subcanonical_fpqcTopology` in the `Presheaf.IsSheaf` form in
which the sheaf condition is stated. -/
@[sga "3 IV 6.3.1" "(iii), special case"]
theorem isSheaf_fpqc_yoneda_obj (a : BigFppfOver B S hS) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf (Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage.comap (toScheme B S hS)).toGrothendieck
      (yoneda.obj a) :=
  (isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type _ _).2
    (GrothendieckTopology.Subcanonical.isSheaf_of_isRepresentable _)

variable {B S hS}

/-- **A fibre product of fpqc sheaves along a representable, formed in presheaves, is an fpqc
sheaf.** This is the fpqc counterpart of
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isSheaf_pullback_yoneda_obj`, and it is the shape in which the
descent arguments consume the sheaf condition of a representable. -/
theorem isSheaf_fpqc_pullback_yoneda_obj {X Y : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (f : X ⟶ Y)
    {a : BigFppfOver B S hS} (h : yoneda.obj a ⟶ Y)
    (hX : Presheaf.IsSheaf
      (Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage.comap (toScheme B S hS)).toGrothendieck X)
    (hY : Presheaf.IsSheaf
      (Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage.comap (toScheme B S hS)).toGrothendieck Y) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf (Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage.comap (toScheme B S hS)).toGrothendieck
      (pullback f h) :=
  Presheaf.isSheaf_pullback _ f h hX (isSheaf_fpqc_yoneda_obj B S hS a) hY

end BigFppfOver

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
